{"story_id":"PH-12814-060","title":"The Spider and the Fly","title_raw":"The Spider and the Fly","notes":"","language":"en","original_language":"und","country":"Philippines","country_code":"PH","culture_region":"フィリピン","latitude":12.8,"longitude":121.8,"location_precision":"culture_region","map_location_type":"source_culture_region","collector":"Mabel Cook Cole","translator":null,"publication_year":1916,"year_evidence":"扉に『Philippine Folk Tales / Compiled and Annotated by / Mabel Cook Cole / 1916』","book_id":"PG-12814","book_title":"Philippine Folk Tales","source_provider":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/12814","source_title":"Philippine Folk Tales","license_status":"PUBLIC_DOMAIN_US","license_name":"Public Domain (United States)","license_jurisdiction":"US","rights_evidence_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/12814","redistribution_allowed":true,"commercial_use":true,"derivative_use":true,"ml_processing_status":"reviewed","verification_date":"2026-09-22","word_count":135,"text":"_Visayan_\n\nMr. Spider wanted to marry Miss Fly. Many times he told her of his\nlove and begged her to become his wife, but she always refused for\nshe did not like him.\n\nOne day when she saw Mr. Spider coming again Miss Fly closed all\nthe doors and windows of her house and made ready a pot of boiling\nwater. Then she waited, and when Mr. Spider called, begging her\nto allow him to enter, she answered by throwing boiling water at\nhim. This made Mr. Spider very angry and he cried:\n\n\"I will never forgive you for this, but I and my descendants will\nalways despise you. We will never give you any peace.\"\n\nMr. Spider kept his word, and even today one can see the hatred of\nthe spider for the fly.","cluster":54,"paragraphs":["_Visayan_","Mr. Spider wanted to marry Miss Fly. Many times he told her of his love and begged her to become his wife, but she always refused for she did not like him.","One day when she saw Mr. Spider coming again Miss Fly cl